  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "read",
    "description": "Read a file as \"ID§code\" lines. The ID names the line for edit and stays fixed across edits; it is not a line number. pattern: only matching lines plus context, enough to edit without a full read. With a directory path and pattern, searches every file in it (glob narrows, e.g. \"*.py\"). symbol: a name's definition plus every line that mentions it, across the directory. Use instead of Read/Grep: results carry IDs, so you can edit straight from them."
   },
   {
    "name": "edit",
    "description": "Edit by the IDs from read (the number before §, never a line number); batch all edits in one call (they all refer to the file as last read). {from, to?, text}: replace lines from..to (text \"\" deletes). {after|before, text}: insert. {find, replace, from?, to?}: substring replace in those lines (IDs, or line numbers from Grep), or the whole file without from; no read needed. With a directory path, find/replace edits apply to every file containing find (glob narrows): a multi-file rename in one call. {text} alone on a new path creates the file; {rename: newPath} moves it, IDs kept; {delete: true} removes it; these three only inside the project. text is raw code without IDs. Returns the new lines with their IDs and a syntax check."
   }
  ],
